        regionalContext: {
          id: 'regional-context',
          title: 'Why CPU-Only LLMs Matter for Privacy-Sensitive Deployments',
          content: [
            '**EU / GDPR:** when a model runs offline on your own CPU, prompts and documents do not have to leave the device, which for many small teams is a technically straightforward way to avoid third-country transfer questions under Art. 44 GDPR. Whether GDPR, the EU AI Act or other obligations apply depends on who deploys the system and for what purpose; this guide is not legal advice, and overall compliance depends on your full setup, not the inference architecture alone.',
            '**Offline and low-connectivity environments:** CPU models work without a reliable internet connection. A model file such as Phi-4 Mini that you download once can run without further network access, which helps in regions with unstable connectivity or metered bandwidth.',
          ],
        },
        commonMistakes: {
          id: 'common-mistakes',
          title: 'What Are the Common CPU Inference Mistakes?',
          items: [
            '**Running FP16 instead of Q4_K_M.** An FP16 Phi-4 Mini file is about 7.6 GB versus 2.5 GB at Q4_K_M, so the bandwidth ceiling drops from about 20 to about 7 tok/s on dual-channel DDR4-3200. Use quantized GGUF models for CPU inference.',
            '**Forgetting to force CPU-only in llama.cpp.** Without explicit flags, a GPU build may offload layers. Set `--n-gpu-layers 0` for pure CPU mode.',
            '**Running one RAM stick.** A single memory channel halves peak bandwidth, so the same model generates at roughly half the speed. Install two matching sticks before buying a faster CPU.',
            '**Choosing too large a model.** Phi-4 Mini (2.5 GB, ceiling about 20 tok/s on dual-channel DDR4-3200) is far more comfortable for interactive use than DeepSeek-R1 7B (4.7 GB, ceiling about 11 tok/s). Match model size to memory bandwidth, not just to free RAM.',
            '**Using the wrong Ollama tag.** `ollama run phi` loads Phi-2, not Phi-4 Mini. Use `ollama run phi4-mini`, and check [ollama.com/library](https://ollama.com/library) for exact model tags.',
          ],
        },
